rustc's wasm-ld linker for wasm32 Linux with side modules (wasm32-unknown-linux-musl): a program is
linked as the guest's C compiler links one (table base 3, exported table, 8 MiB stack, compiler-rt);
a dylib, cdylib or proc macro is a WebAssembly side module (dylink.0) that the C library's dlopen
loads: position-independent, bound to itself, importing what it does not define, without a C
library of its own, its unwinder its own (libgcc_s, which there is not, means libunwind.a).

diff -ruN a/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/linker.rs b/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/linker.rs
--- a/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/linker.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/linker.rs
